WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
In the small city of Armagh, two
cathedrals stand on two hills.

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.210
Both are named after Patrick.

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.430
Two archbishops there
each hold the same title:

4
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.820
Primate of All Ireland.

5
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.850
Yet in Patrick's own writings,
Armagh is never mentioned.

6
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.000
He names no church at all.

7
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.600
So how did Armagh become the
head church of all Ireland?

8
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.790
In this mission, you'll
examine Armagh's great claims,

9
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.940
one source at a time,
and see how they spread.

10
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:32.870
Then you'll weigh up whether
those claims were valid,

11
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.570
and what valid even means here.

12
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:40.520
Your mission: explain how Armagh
became the head church of all Ireland.
